/**
Attributes that are present and empty.

An attribute whose value is falsy is left out — that is what makes
`[hidden=cond]` disappear when `cond` is false. It also means a plain `""`
cannot say "present, with an empty value", and some attributes need to: an
`<option value="">` is the placeholder entry of a select, and dropping its
value changes what the form submits.

`@empty` is that value. It is `gadx.EMPTY`, a value of its own type, never
falsy, which the attribute renderer writes as `name=""`:

- **`[value=@empty]`** — `value=""`.
- **`[value=""]`** — omitted, like any other falsy value.
- **`<option value="">`** — inline HTML means what HTML means, so a literal
  empty value there is present and empty.

`gad fmt` writes it back as `@empty`, since a bare `""` would mean the opposite.
**/

@main
    label Filter

    select[name="kind"]
        // The placeholder: present, with an empty value, so submitting it
        // sends "kind=".
        option[value=@empty] Any kind
        option[value="finish-carpentry"] Finish carpentry
        option[value="kitchen-bath"] Kitchen & bath

    // A falsy value is still dropped: this renders as a bare <div>.
    div[data-note=""] omitted

    // Inline HTML keeps an empty value, the way a browser reads it.
    <select name="inline"><option value="">Any</option></select>
